      "cooked": "<p>IV:\n\n\n<span>When this card enters play, destroy all other Distortion cards. Each Ongoing and Equipment card now has a maximum HP of 6.</span></p><p>LL:\n\n\n<span>Whenever a Villain card would be destroyed, reveal the top card of the Villain deck. If it is not a Lucky card, discard it and prevent the card destruction. If it is a Lucky card, put it into play.</span></p><p>So, Kismet doesn't normally have targets in her deck, but IV can change that.&nbsp; What happens when the heroes reduce one of her Ongoings to &lt;=0 HP when LL is in play and you reveal a non-Lucky card?</p><p>I *think* that you 'prevent' the destruction, but since it still has &lt;=0 HP, it is immediately destroyed again.&nbsp; So, basically, you'd keep revealing and discarding non-Lucky cards until you got a Lucky one.&nbsp;</p><p>Thoughts?</p>",
